# ConfirmAgentPlan.srv - Post-user-confirmation trusted Agent call. NOT a way
# to turn verbal confirmation into authorize_motion.
#
# See docs/lightweight_skill_package_registry_design_zh.md section 11.6.
#
# The Agent must first generate a fresh task_id and present the user with the
# plan kind, ordered steps, typed parameters, exact snapshot identity and that
# task_id; only after explicit user confirmation may the CLI call this service.
# The coordinator/plan store must atomically validate
# (plan_token, plan_digest, task_id, registry_epoch, registry_generation,
# registry_digest), transition the plan from PLANNED to CONFIRMED and return a
# single-use confirmation_token bound to that exact tuple. Mismatch, duplicate
# confirmation, expired plan or reload-changed identity all fail closed.
#
# confirmation_token does not grant motion authorization, does not hold the
# root lease and does not enter any digest; it only proves that this exact
# plan/task pair has been confirmed once. schema_version is 1 in v1.

uint32 schema_version
string plan_token
string plan_digest
string task_id
string registry_epoch
uint64 registry_generation
string registry_digest
---
bool confirmed
string confirmation_token
string error_code
string message
SkillDiagnostic[] diagnostics
